## 8. Deviation handling

Deviations shall be managed according to WI-016.

All deviations shall:

- Receive a unique DEV identifier.
- Be assessed for impact.
- Be documented before protocol closure.
- Be dispositioned before MVR approval.

Acceptance criteria will not be modified after test execution.

Failed acceptance criteria require documented disposition through the approved quality process.

---

## Role assignment rule

Use exactly DIRECTOR, Project Manager / Quality Coordinator, Software Quality Engineer and Software Engineer; record actual contributor identity separately.

The Software Engineer executes validation activities and retains evidence.

The Software Quality Engineer performs independent review and does not approve work.

Only the DIRECTOR may approve protocols, reports, validation conclusions, releases, tags, and gates.

